        id: 47,
        title: "The media: in print",
        theory: `
        <div class="theory-section academic-forest">
            <div class="study-zone">
                <div class="theory-block">
                    <div class="theory-header">
                        <div class="theory-letter">A</div>
                        <h3>Newspaper sections / Gazeta bo'limlari</h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="web-text glossary-list">
                        <p><strong>editorial / leader</strong> <em>(bosh maqola)</em> — an article giving the newspaper's opinion</p>
                        <p><strong>obituary</strong> <em>(ta'ziya xabari)</em> — a report about someone who has recently died</p>
                        <p><strong>classified ads</strong> <em>(e'lonlar)</em> — small advertisements organised by category</p>
                        <p><strong>supplement</strong> <em>(qo'shimcha jurnal)</em> — a separate magazine included free with a newspaper</p>
                        <p><strong>agony aunt</strong> <em>(maslahatchi)</em> — a person who replies to readers' personal problems in a magazine</p>
                        <p><strong>feature</strong> <em>(maxsus maqola)</em> — a longer article focusing on a particular topic</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="theory-block">
                    <div class="theory-header">
                        <div class="theory-letter">B</div>
                        <h3>Journalism / Jurnalistika</h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="web-text glossary-list">
                        <p><strong>tabloid</strong> <em>(tabloid)</em> — a newspaper with short articles, large photos, often sensational</p>
                        <p><strong>broadsheet</strong> <em>(katta formatli gazeta)</em> — a serious newspaper with detailed reporting</p>
                        <p><strong>circulation</strong> <em>(tarqalish)</em> — the number of copies of a newspaper sold</p>
                        <p><strong>readership</strong> <em>(o'quvchilar soni)</em> — the total number of people who read a publication</p>
                        <p><strong>scoop</strong> <em>(sensatsion xabar)</em> — an important news story reported before any other media</p>
                        <p><strong>headline</strong> <em>(sarlavha)</em> — the title of a newspaper article in large print</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="theory-block">
                    <div class="theory-header">
                        <div class="theory-letter">C</div>
                        <h3>Press issues / Matbuot masalalari</h3>
                    </div>
                    <div class="theory-text-column">
                        <p class="web-text">
                            <strong>Press freedom</strong> <em>(matbuot erkinligi)</em> is the right of newspapers to publish without government control. <strong>Libel</strong> <em>(tuhmat)</em> is publishing false statements that damage someone's reputation. <strong>Paparazzi</strong> <em>(paparazzi)</em> are photographers who follow celebrities. <strong>Bias</strong> <em>(noxolislik)</em> means unfairly favouring one side.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>`,
